glm-5.3 and glm-5.3-flash on --provider zai now use yoagent's own preset: a 1,000,000-token window and max_tokens = 128000, instead of the guessed 128K / 4096. Build, all tests, clippy and fmt pass, and the change is committed as 533781cb (not pushed yet).

Built binary (fresh HOME, dummy key, `--provider zai --model glm-5.3`):
• Before: it printed "Unknown model 'glm-5.3'… Known models: glm-4-plus, glm-4-air, glm-4-flash" and "no preset is known… max_tokens = 4096".
• After: neither line prints.
• One character off (`glm-5.4`): both warnings still print, and the known-models list now ends with "glm-5.3, glm-5.3-flash".

What changed:
• `src/agent_builder.rs`: vendor_preset now asks yoagent's ModelConfig::preset instead of four hand-typed arms. It does this only for google, xai, mistral and zai, which are listed in a new VENDOR_PRESET_PROVIDERS. The zai arm now takes the preset's window, max_tokens, cost and reasoning, but keeps its own URL and wire settings, and a user --base-url still wins. Function names and signatures are unchanged, and the file stayed at 4962 lines.
• `src/providers.rs`: any yoagent preset id now counts as a known model. The new known_model_ids_with_presets adds yoagent's ids for that provider to the end of the existing list, so the first five ids the other providers show are unchanged.
• `src/cli.rs`: the "Unknown model" warning reads that list. This one-line swap is outside the planned file list.
• New `src/vendor_preset_tests.rs`, registered in `src/main.rs`:
  • every yoagent preset must resolve to its own limits or be listed in PRESETS_NOT_YET_ROUTED with a reason; a listed id that starts matching fails the test, so the list can only shrink
  • every preset id is a known model
  • glm-5.3 keeps the Z.ai endpoint
  • near-miss ids and other providers keep the guessed limits
• `docs/src/configuration/models.md`: updated to cover the two GLM ids.

Census before the change (yoyo vs yoagent): no routed provider had different numbers, so nothing needed choosing. The four arms I removed matched the preset exactly, and the existing vendor-number tests were not touched and still pass.

| Preset ids | Result |
|---|---|
| anthropic (9), openai gpt-6-* / gpt-6.1-sol, google (2), grok-4.7, mistral-large-4 | identical |
| zai glm-5.3, glm-5.3-flash | 128000/4096 vs 1000000/128000, now routed |
| openai gpt-5.5 | 128000/4096 vs 1000000/64000, not routed |
| qwen qwen3.8-max, qwen3.8-flash | 128000/4096 vs 1000000/131072, not routed |

Positive control: I made the preset lookup return nothing and two of the new tests failed by name. I restored it in the same command, and all four pass again.

Left out on purpose (also listed in the commit):
• `anthropic_preset`: still needs the -YYYYMMDD dated-id handling pinned both ways. Its nine ids already resolve to the same numbers.
• `openai_preset` / `gpt-5.5`: routing it means deciding the Responses-vs-Chat-Completions wire question (#1060 item 1).
• qwen: yoyo has no qwen provider at all, so its two presets have nowhere to land yet.
• Default models: unchanged; zai still defaults to glm-4-plus.

